  "task": "Assess the resilience of the 'telemetry-pipeline' stack in eu-west-1 against an Availability Zone failure and against a full Region failure, and identify the single highest-priority fix.",
  "context": "User ingests device telemetry via a CloudFormation stack named 'telemetry-pipeline' in eu-west-1. They want to understand the blast radius / impact if one AZ fails or if the whole eu-west-1 region fails, and what the top remediation priority should be.",
  "resources": ["telemetry-pipeline (CloudFormation stack, eu-west-1)"],
  "timeframe": "current state (not historical incident) - this is a point-in-time architecture/resilience assessment",
  "criteria": "1) Enumerate the stack's resources (ingestion layer e.g. Kinesis/SQS/API Gateway/ALB, compute e.g. Lambda/ECS/EC2, storage e.g. DynamoDB/S3/RDS/Aurora, any queues or buffers). 2) For each, determine AZ resilience: is it inherently multi-AZ (e.g. S3, DynamoDB, Kinesis) or does it depend on explicit multi-AZ config (e.g. RDS Multi-AZ, ASG spanning subnets/AZs, number of AZs used by subnets)? Flag anything pinned to a single AZ or single subnet. 3) Determine Region resilience: is there any cross-region replication, backup, or DR setup (S3 CRR, DynamoDB global tables, RDS cross-region read replica, Route53 failover)? If none found, call that out explicitly - most pipelines have no region failover by default. 4) Identify data loss / availability impact in each failure scenario (e.g. would telemetry be dropped, buffered and retried, or lost permanently). 5) Recommend the single highest-priority fix to improve resilience, with brief reasoning, plus 1-2 secondary suggestions."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Assess AZ/Region failure resilience of telemetry-pipeline CloudFormation stack in eu-west-1"}], "created_at": null}

